  "description": "Qal\u2019eh-i Imam (\u201cImam Fortress\u201d), also call Qal\u2019eh-i Marivan (\u201cMarivan Fortress\u201d), is one of the most important castles and fortresses in the Kurdistan Province, Marivan District, Iran. This now-ruined military fortification played a key role during the Safavid Period (1502\u20131737) and was an administrative venter of Ardalanians and Babanians rulers in Kurdistan. The discovery of a stele fragment of the Assyrian king Sargon II (r. 721\u2013705 BC) in the drystone wall enclosing one of the buildings of the village Barqaleh might attest to a settlement there in the eighth century BC.",
